<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Dictyostelium discoideum Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 2.304 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 72.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 integrates Schnakenberg kinetics on an 11.52 µm periodic cell so the discrete-Laplacian growth rate peaks at 2.304 µm (measured 2.3037 µm). The GIF is a 12-frame, 960×720 activator field. The public-domain sorocarp is the species photograph, not a cortical micrograph. Diffusion-ratio sweep, equal-diffusion ablation, specimen segmentation, and dispersion goodness-of-fit are left for the v2 re-score. Overall 72.8/100 (faithfulness 68.1, reproducibility 83.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 84, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 64, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: docs/media/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dictyostelium-discoideum-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 292818 B, 1584×984 px, artifact_sha256 bac77ec104f165d2016729fc8ed5760b374a6e3b832ae85a3aa36ecf78caaba4 (sha256 bac77ec104f165d2016729fc8ed5760b374a6e3b832ae85a3aa36ecf78caaba4), spec_fingerprint 960dc004eb4baeba25b2cb4a7d5ced2a0307317641afcb7da587f46f715075d8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 960dc004eb4baeba25b2cb4a7d5ced2a0307317641afcb7da587f46f715075d8; artifact_sha256: bac77ec104f165d2016729fc8ed5760b374a6e3b832ae85a3aa36ecf78caaba4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=b4d3f1e6feedaad3..., datasets/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0/dictyostelium_discoideum_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=e2d2b739211bda97...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber. | Taniguchi 2013: Dictyostelium PIP3 and F-actin travel as cortical excitable waves. | Höfer, Sherratt and Maini 1995: cAMP relay plus chemotaxis produces aggregation streams.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg PDE with a=0.16, b=0.94, Du=0.03208776235376616, Dv=0.770106296490388, periodic 80×80 grid, seed 3168.; transfer_boundary: Catalog wavelength 2.304 µm (2.304e-06 m, log10=-5.638, tier 3_subcellular_um) is the slot coordinate inside the cortical-wave band, not a printed wet-lab mean. | Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. A 0.20 µm molecular regime admits zero modes; millimetre-scale cAMP waves are a longer regime of the same extant species.; does_not_claim: That sorocarps are pigment stripes or ocelli. | That the phase-singularity model of Taniguchi 2013 was integrated.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R-ablation: score the equal-diffusion negative control (variance collapse versus the δ=24 run).",
        "remediation needed: R-assessor: a second assessor did not score this pass.",
        "remediation needed: R-cv: enter the real specimen border-contrast segmentation (foreground, circularity, coherency) as morphometrics with references that are not equal to the measured values.",
        "remediation needed: R-gof: report Pearson r, RMSE, and KS for the dispersion relation, plus the specimen-versus-GIF orientation KS.",
        "remediation needed: R-sweep: score the δ = Dv/Du sweep (onset and the monotonic rise of λ once σ_max > 0) under parameter-expressivity." ;
    pk:hasScore 7.28e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

